# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, also on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true, so scripts, workflows and generated files are byte-identical on
# every machine. PowerShell scripts are the one exception: Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads
# them most reliably with CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.psm1 text eol=crlf
*.psd1 text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.syso binary
*.msi binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.pdf binary
